  "summary": "South San Francisco announced the launch of an automated license plate recognition program with 28 solar-powered Flock Safety cameras at key public locations, aimed at addressing property crime, particularly in the hotel corridor. Police Chief Scott Campbell called the technology a 'game changer,' and the city said each search requires justification and data will not be sold or shared with third parties.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The use of this technology has already proven to be a game changer in the fight against crime and a valuable tool for our officers to help solve otherwise difficult-to-solve cases",
      "paragraph_idx": 2
    },
    {
      "quote": "Each search requires a justification, and the data is never sold or shared with third parties.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    }
  ],
